<div class="content-block">
    <p>Every web application has two structures: the one visible through its navigation menu, and the one that actually exists on the server. Enumeration is the process of discovering that second, larger structure by systematically testing paths a site never advertises, such as forgotten admin panels, leftover backup files, and API routes that no link on the page ever points to.</p>

    <p>By the end of this room, you will understand how attackers and security professionals map a target's true attack surface, and you will complete a hands-on simulation where you use a directory scanner to uncover hidden paths on a fictional site.</p>

