// TASK 2: Mapping a Web Application
$task_contents[2] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <h2>Beyond the Navigation Bar</h2>

    <p>A site's navigation bar only shows what its developers chose to link. Enumeration assumes there is more, and sets out to find it by systematically requesting paths that might exist even though nothing points to them.</p>

    <p>This is done with a wordlist, a large text file containing common directory and file names collected from real world applications. An enumeration tool requests each entry from the list against the target and records how the server responds.</p>

    <div class="info-box">
        <h4><i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> Stay Within Scope</h4>
        <p>Enumeration should only ever be performed against systems you own or have explicit written authorization to test. Scanning a target without permission is illegal in most jurisdictions.</p>
    </div>

    <h3>Reading the Response</h3>
    <p>Every request the tool sends gets a status code back. That code tells you whether the path is worth investigating further.</p>

    <table class="content-table">
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Status Code</th>
                <th>Meaning</th>
                <th>Enumeration Significance</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td>200</td>
                <td>OK</td>
                <td>The path exists and returned content. Worth exploring.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>301 / 302</td>
                <td>Redirect</td>
                <td>The path exists but points elsewhere. Follow the redirect.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>403</td>
                <td>Forbidden</td>
                <td>The path exists but access is blocked. Confirms the resource is real.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td>404</td>
                <td>Not Found</td>
                <td>The path does not exist on the server. Discard and move on.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- SVG: request/response enumeration cycle
