    <h2>What the Navigation Bar Does Not Tell You</h2>

    <p>A page does not need to be linked to be reachable. If you know or guess its exact URL, the server will serve it whether or not any menu points to it. These are called unlinked pages, and developers often leave them behind unintentionally.</p>

    <p>Staging pages, old versions of a site, internal testing tools, and forgotten features are common examples. None of them were meant to be public, but none of them are actually protected either.</p>

