    <h2>The Kitchen Behind the Menu</h2>

    <p>Modern applications are usually built on top of an API that the visible pages quietly call in the background. A customer only sees the menu, but the kitchen behind it has its own full system of orders, ingredients, and staff. The API is that hidden system.</p>

    <p>API routes are rarely linked anywhere. Instead they are called directly by JavaScript running in the browser, which means the routes exist in that JavaScript code even if no human ever sees a link to them.</p>

