$task_contents[8] = <<<'HTML'
<div class="content-block">
    <p>You now understand that a web application's true structure extends far beyond its navigation bar. Enumeration is the systematic process of uncovering that structure, from hidden pages and predictable admin panels to leaked backup files and undocumented API routes.</p>

    <p>These same techniques form the first stage of nearly every real world security assessment, because you cannot secure or attack what you do not know exists.</p>

    <h3>Key Takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
        <li>Enumeration systematically tests paths using a wordlist rather than guessing at random.</li>
        <li>HTTP status codes such as 200, 301, 403, and 404 reveal whether a path is worth investigating.</li>
        <li>Unlinked pages and files like robots.txt can reveal a site's hidden structure.</li>
        <li>Admin panels follow predictable naming conventions across common platforms.</li>
        <li>Backup and configuration files often leak credentials that were never meant to be public.</li>
        <li>API routes exist independently of visible pages and are often found inside JavaScript files.</li>
    </ul>
</div>
